<title>GERMANY: Axa German life unit had 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Axa German life unit had 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Axa Leben Versicherung AG, the German life unit of French insurer Axa SA, reported losses for the year to the end of 1996, Axa said at a press conference in Frankfurt on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The company said the unit had a single-digit million mark loss for the period, mainly due to investments in computer technology. Premiums had risen faster than the market average.</p>
<p>Axa board member Gerard de La Martiniere said the group was considering merging Axa Leben with Colonia, the German insurer it acquired through taking over UAP, but that &quot;several scenarios&quot; were being considered.</p>
<p>The aim was to achieve significantly higher profits from German business, he added.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
